   and documentation) is protected by copyright. All rights remain with
   NEO Digital. This license does not sell any rights in the software; it
   grants a right of use.

2. Right of use
   NEO Digital grants a free, non-exclusive and non-transferable right to
   use the software on any number of websites.

   Condition: the legal notice (Impressum / imprint) of every website on which
   the software runs publicly contains the credit "NEO Website Check: NEO Digital"
   linking to https://neo-digital.at. Without the credit, the right of use
   for that website ends.

   Use without the credit, as well as updates, support or other terms,
   requires a separate agreement with NEO Digital.

3. You may
   a) install and configure the software under section 2;
   b) adapt configuration, templates, stylesheets and texts and modify the
      code for your own installations;
   c) as an agency, install it for your clients under section 2.

4. You may not
   a) distribute, publish, rent or sell the software or modified versions,
      except installing it under section 3 c;
   b) grant sublicenses;
   c) offer the software or substantial parts of it as your own product or as
      a service to third parties;
   d) remove or alter copyright and license notices.

5. Third-party components
   Third-party components that are shipped or required (e.g. Contao, Symfony, Dompdf, the Arimo font (SIL Open Font License 1.1))
   are subject to their own licenses.

6. Warranty and liability
   The software is provided free of charge and as is. Liability for slight
   negligence is excluded to the extent permitted by law; personal injury is
   excepted. NEO Digital is not liable for content from external services
   (e.g. answers of an AI model) or for costs incurred with chosen third-party
   providers.

7. Governing law and venue
   Austrian law applies, excluding its conflict-of-law rules and the
   UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. Venue is
   Graz, Austria, to the extent permitted by law.

